        "node_id": "n_1_403e90",
        "thought_text": "The issue lies in the `dfs` function. When the target is not found in the tree, the function should return `True` to indicate a failure, but it currently returns `False`. This causes the `find_failures` function to incorrectly count these cases as successes. To fix this, modify the `dfs` function to return `True` when the target is not found.",
