        "node_id": "n_2_e04553",
        "thought_text": "Revised Thought-1: Instead of using a DFS approach, implement a modified BFS traversal where we track the path taken to reach each node. For each target value, perform the BFS starting from the root. If at any point the path diverges from the expected direction based on the comparison of the current node's value with the target, increment the failure count. This ensures that we accurately simulate the search behavior described in the problem statement, even for non-binary search trees.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_e04553_0",
